            <ArticleTitle>Surgical intradiscal decompression without annulotomy in lumbar disc herniation using a coblation device: preliminary results.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>107-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Annulotomy is a mandatory step to perform intradiscal decompression to resolve a disco radicular conflict. However, this manoeuvre can lead to post surgical complications such as vertebral instability and back pain. Coblation assisted microdiscectomy (CAM procedure) allows a quoted removal of disc without anulus damage.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
